  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nAn upper ridge and Bermuda high pressure will be centered off \nthe coast through Saturday, becoming suppressed late in the \nweekend as shortwave energy pushes across the mid- Atlantic. \nMore of a zonal pattern develops next week with a series of \nshortwave troughs pushing across the area. Precip chances will \nbe near climo each day with widely scattered showers and \nthunderstorms developing each afternoon, then dissipating with \nloss of heating during the evening. The severe threat appears \nminimal through the period with limited shear and forcing. \n\nA gradual warming trend will continue through the period as well\nwith highs in the lower 90s inland through the weekend, then\nwarming in to the mid 90s next week. Temps generally in the mid\nto upper 80s along the coast. The probabilities for Major Heat\nRisk increase to around 60-80% Monday through Thursday of next\nweek.",
